<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34103" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμετ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>provoking sickness</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				36
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς, σπαραττόμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					13.155
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>inclined to vomit</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Acut.</u>
				67
			</span></i>; of certain animals, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				632b11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>one who uses emetics</i>, like the Roman
			gourmands, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pomp.</u>
				51
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμετικὴν</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίαιταν</span>) <i>agebat</i>, he was taking
				<i>a course of emetics</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				13.52.1
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
